ant, preserving high cards for defending against landlord’s bombs or seizing control late is crucial. The landlord has 19 cards—likely has bombs or rockets. Since this is the first trick and the card played is minimal, letting my teammate take it if possible is cooperative and doesn’t reveal my hand strength prematurely. If both peasants pass, landlord gets the trick cheaply, but that’s acceptable early when conserving power.\n\n**Answer:**  \n{"cards": []}'}
